<title>COSTA RICA: ACPC will not relax coffee export plan -- Oliveira.</title>
<headline>ACPC will not relax coffee export plan -- Oliveira.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Costa Rica 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Association of Coffee Producing Countries is not going to relax its export limit program even though coffee prices have been trending upward, the secretary general of the coffee cartel said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We cannot create any feeling that supply is going to be on a more relaxed mood in the coming months because we need a certain stablisation of the market around a relative level,&quot; Roberio Oliveira told Reuters in an interview here at International Coffee Week, known in Spanish as Sintercafe.</p>
</text>
